course: dictionary
lesson: 11584
title: A rare formal word: anteriority
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Some words are long and formal, but you can still work them out. Look at the ending first. The ending -ity turns a word into a noun, a name for a quality or state, so anteriority names a quality. «The anteriority of the first draft shows it was written before the final copy.» The clues are first and before, so anteriority means being earlier in time.
explain: Science texts use the same word in a different way. «In a fish, the anteriority of the head shows where the front of the body is.» Here the clue is front, so in science anteriority means being at the front. Always ask: what simpler words would fit here? Then swap them in and check the sentence still makes sense.
explain: You will rarely hear this word at home or at school. In everyday talk, people say «coming first» or «being earlier». When you meet a rare formal word, do not panic. Find the clues, try a simpler word, and check the dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: Anteriority is a noun: it names a quality or state.
fact: «Anteriority» means being earlier in time than something else.
fact: In science, «anteriority» means being at the front.
fact: It is a formal word, found in grammar, law and science. In everyday talk, say «coming first» or «being earlier».
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «being earlier» or «being at the front» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The anteriority of the first draft shows it was written before the final copy.» What does anteriority mean here? | Being very rare | *Being earlier in time | Being very long | Being at the back
exercise: «In a fish, the anteriority of the head shows where the front of the body is.» What does anteriority mean in science? | *Being at the front | Being underwater | Being in the middle | Being at the back
exercise: Which everyday phrase is closest in meaning to anteriority in «the anteriority of the first map»? | Being round | Being wet | Being loud | *Being earlier
test: «The judge checked the anteriority of the two letters to see which was sent first.» What does anteriority mean here? | Being in a bigger envelope | Being more polite | *Being earlier in time | Being longer
test: Mia says anteriority is just a fancy word for being late. Is she right? | *No, it means being earlier in time or being at the front | Yes, it means being quiet | Yes, it means being late | Yes, it means being in the middle
exam: «The anteriority of the leg is toward the front.» In science, which meaning fits best? | Being very heavy | Being at the back | Being earlier in time | *Being at the front
